# Pipeline templates

Small, ready-made pipelines from the platform team. Each one is a single file
that works in any service made from the golden path, without changes.

| Template | What it does | When it runs |
|---|---|---|
| [workflows/first-pipeline.yaml](workflows/first-pipeline.yaml) | The smallest useful pipeline: gets the code, lists it, runs the tests. A first pipeline to read and copy | On every pull request, and when you click Run Workflow |
| [workflows/smoke-test.yaml](workflows/smoke-test.yaml) | Checks that a running environment of your service answers: its page, its health check, and the environment it reports | When you click Run Workflow (choose dev, staging or prod) |
| [workflows/nightly-scan.yaml](workflows/nightly-scan.yaml) | Scans the image of your latest commit on main again for known weaknesses (CVEs) | Every night at 02:00, and when you click Run Workflow |
| [workflows/security-checks.yaml](workflows/security-checks.yaml) | DevSecOps on every change: SAST with the security team's rules (semgrep), and a scan of the libraries the service lists for known weaknesses (CVEs, trivy). Red on a dangerous line, or on a HIGH or CRITICAL CVE that has a fix | On every pull request, and when you click Run Workflow |
| [workflows/dast.yaml](workflows/dast.yaml) | DAST: attacks a running environment of your service from the outside (path traversal, cross-site scripting, unexpected methods), and reports the protective headers it is missing | When you click Run Workflow (choose dev, staging or prod) |

## Use one

1. Open the template file and copy all of it (the copy button above the file).
2. In your service's repository: **Add File → New File**. Name it
   `.gitea/workflows/<the same file name>`, for example
   `.gitea/workflows/smoke-test.yaml`, and paste.
3. Commit it on a new branch and open a pull request. It is reviewed and
   merged like any other change.
4. After the merge, open the **Actions** tab: the new pipeline is in the list
   on the left. Click it, then **Run Workflow**.

## Where the main pipeline comes from

The pipeline every service already has, `.gitea/workflows/ci.yaml` (lint,
tests, secret scan, build, scan, push, sign), is in the golden-path template,
[platform/golden-path](https://{{ pelab_hosts.gitea }}/{{ golden_path_platform_org }}/{{ golden_path_template_repo }}). Each new service gets a copy of it when
it is created from that template.

## Ask for a change, or a new template

Open an issue in this repository. Please do not change a template in your own
copy: if it needs a fix, everyone needs it.
